## 179. Universal Coding Formula

For letter-position coding:

```text
A = 1
...
Z = 26
```

For a shift:

```text
C = (P + S - 1) mod 26 + 1
```

where:

```text
P = original position
S = shift
C = coded position
```

For reverse alphabet:

```text
C = 27 - P
```

For position-dependent shifts:

```text
Cᵢ = (Pᵢ + Sᵢ - 1) mod 26 + 1
```

